# Captions

All captions use the `Caption` type from `@remotion/captions`:

```ts
type Caption = {
  text: string;
  startMs: number;
  endMs: number;
  timestampMs: number | null;
  confidence: number | null;
};
```

Install: `npx remotion add @remotion/captions`

# Transcribing Audio (Whisper.cpp)

Install: `npx remotion add @remotion/install-whisper-cpp`

```ts
import { installWhisperCpp, downloadWhisperModel, transcribe, toCaptions } from '@remotion/install-whisper-cpp';
import path from 'path';
import fs from 'fs';

const to = path.join(process.cwd(), 'whisper.cpp');
await installWhisperCpp({ to, version: '1.5.5' });
await downloadWhisperModel({ model: 'medium.en', folder: to });

const whisperCppOutput = await transcribe({
  model: 'medium.en',
  whisperPath: to,
  whisperCppVersion: '1.5.5',
  inputPath: '/path/to/audio.wav',  // Convert to 16KHz wav first if needed
  tokenLevelTimestamps: true,
});

const { captions } = toCaptions({ whisperCppOutput });
fs.writeFileSync('captions.json', JSON.stringify(captions, null, 2));
// Move to public/ folder so Remotion can fetch it
```

# Importing .srt Files

```tsx
import { parseSrt } from '@remotion/captions';
import { useDelayRender, staticFile } from 'remotion';

const { delayRender, continueRender, cancelRender } = useDelayRender();
const [handle] = useState(() => delayRender());

useEffect(() => {
  fetch(staticFile('subtitles.srt'))
    .then(r => r.text())
    .then(text => {
      const { captions: parsed } = parseSrt({ input: text });
      setCaptions(parsed);
      continueRender(handle);
    })
    .catch(cancelRender);
}, []);
```

# Displaying Captions (TikTok style)

Put captioning logic in a **separate component file**.

```tsx
import { createTikTokStyleCaptions } from '@remotion/captions';
import { Sequence, useVideoConfig, AbsoluteFill, useCurrentFrame } from 'remotion';

const SWITCH_CAPTIONS_EVERY_MS = 1200;

const { pages } = useMemo(() =>
  createTikTokStyleCaptions({ captions, combineTokensWithinMilliseconds: SWITCH_CAPTIONS_EVERY_MS }),
  [captions]
);

// Render pages as Sequences
const { fps } = useVideoConfig();
{pages.map((page, index) => {
  const nextPage = pages[index + 1] ?? null;
  const startFrame = (page.startMs / 1000) * fps;
  const endFrame = Math.min(
    nextPage ? (nextPage.startMs / 1000) * fps : Infinity,
    startFrame + (SWITCH_CAPTIONS_EVERY_MS / 1000) * fps,
  );
  const durationInFrames = endFrame - startFrame;
  if (durationInFrames <= 0) return null;
  return <Sequence key={index} from={startFrame} durationInFrames={durationInFrames}><CaptionPage page={page} /></Sequence>;
})}
```

## Word highlighting

Use `page.tokens` for word-level highlighting. Use `whiteSpace: "pre"` to preserve whitespace:

```tsx
const frame = useCurrentFrame();
const { fps } = useVideoConfig();
const absoluteTimeMs = page.startMs + (frame / fps) * 1000;

{page.tokens.map((token) => (
  <span
    key={token.fromMs}
    style={{ color: token.fromMs <= absoluteTimeMs && token.toMs > absoluteTimeMs ? '#39E508' : 'white' }}
  >
    {token.text}
  </span>
))}
```

Place captions alongside video content:
```tsx
<AbsoluteFill>
  <Video src={staticFile('video.mp4')} />
  <CaptionPage page={page} />
</AbsoluteFill>
```
